  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "The replicated 2M regression begins after a measurable post-1M turning point and is concentrated in seat0 and Standard10 performance; shared-deck archive evaluation across both seeds can distinguish monotone degradation from a late noisy endpoint and identify whether approximately 1M early stopping is justified.",
  "material_change": "Without new training, evaluate the existing iteration 256, 320, 384, and final approximately 2.1M checkpoints from each seed against its untouched 1M control. Use 2048 pairs per four anchors; reuse the same fresh deck seed within each lineage to enable paired endpoint contrasts, while keeping the two lineage seeds independent.",
  "baseline": "The prior verified 2M-minus-1M result over 131072 hands is -3.2402 +/-3.1547 bb/100, with Standard10 -9.0302 +/-6.7912 and seat0 -7.9224 +/-5.6990; both training and Standard10 preservation audits pass.",
  "source": "Frozen Seed1 archives at iterations 256,320,384 and final SHA 993fe99b; frozen Seed2 archives at iterations 256,320,384 and final SHA c072a966. Controls are the clean 1M checkpoints SHA 6fbbe021 and b5602618.",
